    "https://spalding.edu/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Spalding University Jobs | Careers at Spalding in Louisville, KY Give Visit Us Apply Now Connect with Us About Accreditation Our Mission About Louisville President & Leadership Team Student Achievement Outcomes Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Fast-Track Programs Associate & Certificate Programs Student and Academic Success Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Online Admissions Transfer Admissions Plan a Visit Financial Aid Get Started with Financial Aid Cost of Attendance Net Price Calculator Scholarships Veteran Benefits Campus Life Residence Life Campus Ministry Student Organizations Student Wellness Give Visit Us Apply Now Connect with Us Info for Alumni Athletics Give to Spalding Quick Links News & Blog Events Faculty/Staff Directory Careers Working at Spalding Finding a job that aligns with your values is rare — at Spalding University, it’s the expectation. Spalding jobs are more than positions; they’re opportunities to contribute to something meaningful in the heart of Louisville, Kentucky. Spalding University has been a cornerstone of downtown Louisville for over a century, rooted in the mission of the Sisters of Charity of Nazareth. When you join the Spalding team, you become part of a community that genuinely cares — about students, about each other, and about the city we call home. A Place to Grow Spalding employees have access to professional development opportunities designed to help you advance in your career and deepen your expertise. Whether you’re early in your field or a seasoned professional, Spalding invests in its people. Job Openings ﻿ Equal Opportunity Spalding University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University complies with all federal, state and local equal employment opportunity laws. It is the University’s policy not to discriminate against any individual or group of individuals and to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons regardless of race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, military status, veteran status or other protected status. All job offers are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Contact Human Resources Yolanda Peterson, Notary Employee Experience Specialist ypeterson@spalding.edu (502) 873-4177 901 South Fourth Street,\r\nLouisville, KY 40203 (502) 585-9911 News Events Directory Offices Work at Spalding Title IX Consumer Information Transcripts My Spalding University Catalog © Spalding University 2026"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/A99CE46A67143A8F77A8C7BDEA7155DA/jobs/124973": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Nursing - Didactic You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty Nursing - Didactic Spalding-Republic Academic Center (RAC) - Louisville, KY 40203 Apply Overview Education Level Master's Category Nurse Apply Description The School of Nursing in the College of Health and Natural Sciences of Spalding University, Louisville, Kentucky, established in 1933 and the oldest baccalaureate-nursing program in Kentucky, is currently accepting applications for Adjunct Nursing Faculty (classroom and clinical).  Responsibilities include preparation and teaching didactic and/or clinical courses, assessment and evaluation of students through various modalities (quizzes, exams, skills check-offs or clinical assessments). This is an adjunct, contract non-tenure track appointment. The BSN and MSN Programs are fully accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE). The position will vary by course and program. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES In addition to the policies and procedures contained in the Spalding University Faculty Governance Document , Bylaws of the Faculty Organization of the School of Nursing , and the Policies and Procedures of the School of Nursing, the following duties and responsibilities are assigned to School of Nursing Faculty: Classroom and clinical teaching with a commitment to academic excellence. Scholarly activities and university, professional and community service, as able. Utilization of technology to include web-based/enhanced courses and the use of a variety of other technological strategies, i.e., web-based and/or device apps with specific programs for undergraduate, graduate students and clinical simulation. Develop, implement, manage and monitor the academic progress of nursing students within assigned course(s); Participate, as appropriate, in departmental or program meetings; Participate, as able, in continuing faculty development programs. Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing required Prior teaching experience in a ADN/BSN or MSN program is desired. Current or eligible for Kentucky RN or APRN licensure is required. Current knowledge of nursing practice at program level. Demonstrated commitment to inclusiveness and collegiality in personal and professional work and mentoring students and faculty on the importance of multicultural and multidisciplinary applications Experience in contemporary curriculum development and program development, including a concept-based curriculum, desired, but not required. Leadership in strategic communication, problem solving, and shared governance desired. ** All faculty and staff are required to have the COVID 19 vaccination or submit a medical or religious exemption form to Human Resources. ABOUT SPALDING UNIVERSITY: Spalding University offers a comprehensive package including medical, dental, vision, Spalding matching contribution up to 5% to your 403b/Roth retirement plan, generous Paid Time Off program, Parental Leave, paid holidays, paid life insurance and short-term disability, paid time for volunteering, free gym membership, and more. Situated in the heart of downtown Louisville, Kentucky’s largest city, Spalding University combines a rich social justice history and a commitment to community service as we attract students who desire a high-quality education in a very personalized setting. An engaged faculty serves nearly 2300 students at the bachelors’, masters and doctoral levels, providing real-world learning in liberal and professional studies. Faculty, staff and students are united by the institutional mission: Spalding University is a diverse community of learners dedicated to meeting the needs of the times in the tradition of the Sisters of Charity of Nazareth through quality undergraduate and graduate liberal and professional studies, grounded in spiritual values, with an emphasis on service and the promotion of peace and justice. With a focus on service and leadership, Spalding offers all students a mission-driven connection to community and comprehensive learning resources while striking a distinctive balance serving the educational needs of both the traditional student and the working student. In addition, our unique 8-week class delivery format affords students scheduling flexibility amidst other life responsibilities. Spalding aspires to become the first choice for students of compassion and service, with a commitment to our mission, celebrated for a rigorous yet nurturing environment, emulated for interdisciplinary, collaborations, and acclaimed for contributions to the community. Spalding University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University complies with all federal, state and local equal employment opportunity laws. It is the University’s policy not to discriminate against any individual or group of individuals and to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons regardless of race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, military status, veteran status or other protected status. All job offers are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/A99CE46A67143A8F77A8C7BDEA7155DA/jobs/124966": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor (Clinical)",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor (Clinical) - Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor (Clinical) - Nursing Apply Overview Education Level Bachelor's Category Education Apply Description POSITION TITLE Adjunct Nursing Clinical Instructor JOB LOCATION: ___ Fully Remote _ _ _ Hybrid (Some remote work some on campus work) _X_ On Site JOB SUMMARY Clinical instructors are responsible for the instruction and supervision of Spalding University School of Nursing students in clinical and lab settings. Responsibilities of clinical instructors include but are not limited to daily clinical assignments, evaluation of students, and appropriate documentation. Clinical instructors work collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff to support Spalding Universitys mission of serving a diverse community of learners. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Spalding University Prelicensure Nursing Faculty will: Directly/ indirectly supervise students in diverse clinical settings. Attend scheduled meetings with BSN program director, clinical coordinator, and/or course faculty to ensure an understanding of clinical instructor and student responsibilities and objectives. Maintain an open line of communication and collaborate with course faculty throughout the course session. Prepare for clinical experiences by meeting all facility onboarding requirements and reviewing all course documents prior to the first clinical day. Conduct clinical orientation for student groups to orient students to expectations during clinical opportunities. Clinical requirements will be determined by course faculty and facility educators, with input from the clinical instructor. Instruct students and assess performance in the clinical and/or lab setting. Documentation is provided to course faculty and students in a timely manner. Necessary documentation may include: feedback on student assignments, skills, and critical thinking; student attendance and professionalism; formative and summative evaluation including critical thinking and student outcomes. Assign clinical experiences to meet outcome objectives of the course, taking into consideration individual student learning needs. Clinical focus is to be related to didactic learning experiences whenever possible. Provide feedback on students progress, in a timely manner, to facilitate academic success. For students demonstrating difficulties, work with course faculty to offer coaching and counseling. Report any unusual occurrences to the facility and course faculty as appropriate. Notify students, the clinical site, course faculty, and the clinical coordinator as soon as possible for emergency cancellation of a clinical experience. Missed clinical time will be made up at the discretion of the clinical coordinator and course faculty. Leaving the clinical area early is not permitted. Participate in evaluation of the clinical agency/unit and make recommendations to improve future clinical opportunities. Adhere to program, school of nursing, and university policies and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications SKILLS AND EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS Maintain an active, unencumbered Kentucky or Compact Nursing License. In accordance with Kentucky Board of Nursing (KBN) regulations (Section 201 KAR 20:310): A clinical instructor should be a registered nurse with a bachelors degree or higher in nursing from an accredited college or university and have 2 years of full time or equivalent experience as a registered nurse within the immediate past 5 years with evidence of clinical competence appropriate to teaching responsibilities. Maintain professional development/ growth according to personal needs and requirements for certifications/ licensure through practice that directly relates to nursing education (i.e., direct patient care, educational consultation, etc.). INTERRELATIONS Spalding University Prelicensure Clinical Instructors will: Foster a climate of equity and belonging through multicultural awareness and responsiveness while maintaining a commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and collaboration. Work collegially and professionally with students, university employees and external partners. Communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community partners. CONTACT All application are made through the Paycom Applicant Tracking System. **It is highly recommended that all faculty and staff have the COVID 19 vaccination. ABOUT SPALDING UNIVERSITY: Spalding University offers a comprehensive package including medical, dental, vision, Spalding matching contribution up to 5% to your 403b/Roth retirement plan, generous Paid Time Off program, Parental Leave, paid holidays, paid life insurance and short-term disability, paid time for volunteering, free gym membership, and more. Situated in the heart of downtown Louisville, Kentucky’s largest city, Spalding University combines a rich social justice history and a commitment to community service as we attract students who desire a high-quality education in a very personalized setting. An engaged faculty serves nearly 2300 students at the bachelors’, masters and doctoral levels, providing real-world learning in liberal and professional studies. Faculty, staff and students are united by the institutional mission: Spalding University is a diverse community of learners dedicated to meeting the needs of the times in the tradition of the Sisters of Charity of Nazareth through quality undergraduate and graduate liberal and professional studies, grounded in spiritual values, with an emphasis on service and the promotion of peace and justice. With a focus on service and leadership, Spalding offers all students a mission-driven connection to community and comprehensive learning resources while striking a distinctive balance serving the educational needs of both the traditional student and the working student. In addition, our unique 8-week class delivery format affords students scheduling flexibility amidst other life responsibilities. Spalding aspires to become the first choice for students of compassion and service, with a commitment to our mission, celebrated for a rigorous yet nurturing environment, emulated for interdisciplinary, collaborations, and acclaimed for contributions to the community. Spalding University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University complies with all federal, state and local equal employment opportunity laws. It is the University’s policy not to discriminate against any individual or group of individuals and to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons regardless of race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, military status, veteran status or other protected status. All job offers are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/A99CE46A67143A8F77A8C7BDEA7155DA/jobs/309802": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, School of Professional Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, School of Professional Psychology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty, School of Professional Psychology Spalding-Mansion - Louisville, KY 40203 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Master's Category Education Apply Description Adjunct Professor, School of Professional Psychology JOB LOCATION: On Campus JOB SUMMARY Spalding University's School of Professional Psychology invites applications for adjunct professors to teach undergraduate classes. Contracts may be renewed for additional terms based on departmental needs, funding ability, and candidate performance. A minimum of a Master’s degree in Psychology is required. The School of Professional Psychology offers a Bachelor of Science in Psychology with undergraduate major options. For information about the department, visit: https://spalding.edu/psychology/bachelor-of-arts-in-psychology/ DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Teaching classes within a eight week format Serving as part of the Psychology teaching team Qualifications SKILLS AND EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS Masters in Psychology Teaching experience in higher education is preferred INTERRELATIONS Regular or daily contact with administration, faculty, staff, and students. Regular contact with the general public. Must have an appreciation and respect for diverse populations. CONTACT All applications are made through the Paycom Applicant Tracking System. For questions, please reach out to: Dr. Allison Fowler Undergraduate Program Director - School of Professional Psychology afowler02@spalding.edu ABOUT SPALDING UNIVERSITY: Situated in the heart of downtown Louisville, Kentucky’s largest city, Spalding University combines a rich social justice history and a commitment to community service as we attract students who desire a high-quality education in a very personalized setting. An engaged faculty serves nearly 2,000 students at the bachelors’, master’s and doc